Interactive USD edits of an ArnoldGinstance prim

An ArnoldGinstance prim instances a red cube placed out of the frame. The ginstance is moved, its inherit_xform
parameter is enabled and disabled, its visibility is set to 0 and restored, and it instances another cube. The stage
is re-rendered after each edit. Covers the fix of the interactive changes of ArnoldGinstance prims (#2532).
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural (hydra reader) reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive
render session, and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the procedural render of the
"visibility restored" step is compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are
reported as warnings (known issues in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
